<%# locals: (showcase: nil, live_html: nil, sim: nil, sim_frames: [])

    A CSS laptop (screen bezel, hinge, a thin base) showing a contest's live
    page: LaptopFictionalShowcase's FICTIONAL contest, rendered by
    LaptopLiveSnapshot (pages/_laptop_live) and scaled from a 1280 x 800 canvas
    (0.33125). Never a real contest or player, and the same on every date.

    MOSTLY SEEN, PARTLY COVERED. /turf-monster-v2 sets the laptop behind the
    phone, the phone's right third over its left bezel, and lets it run off
    the hero's right edge, which clips it (overflow-hidden on the hero
    section).

    DECORATIVE AND INERT. aria-hidden takes it out of the accessibility tree,
    and `inert` takes the snapshot's links out of the tab order and the
    pointer path. The figure's caption carries the text alternative.

    ITS FEATURED GAME IS SIMULATED (LaptopScoreSimulation): it opens at 3-7 and
    pages/_laptop_score_sim plays a touchdown every ten seconds through the
    live page's own script.

    With no snapshot (a template render with no controller), the screen is
    left blank. %>
<div class="w-[28rem]" aria-hidden="true" inert data-test="laptop-mock">
  <div class="rounded-t-2xl bg-neutral-800 p-3 shadow-[0_24px_64px_-12px_rgb(0_0_0_/_0.35)] ring-1 ring-white/10">
    <div class="aspect-[16/10] overflow-hidden rounded-md bg-page text-body" data-test="laptop-screen">
      <% if showcase && live_html %>
        <%# The canvas: the live page at a 1280 x 800 desktop size (the screen's
            16:10), scaled to the screen's width (28rem less the 0.75rem bezels
            = 26.5rem = 424px; 424 / 1280 = 0.33125). Desktop layout, because
            Tailwind's breakpoints read the viewport; the screen is a fixed
            16:10 box with overflow-hidden, so anything past it is clipped,
            never squeezed. The HTML is LaptopLiveSnapshot's signed-out render. %>
        <div class="w-[1280px] origin-top-left scale-[0.33125]" data-test="laptop-canvas">
          <%= live_html %>
          <% if sim %>
            <%= render "pages/laptop_score_sim", contest: showcase.contest, sim: sim, frames: sim_frames %>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="h-1.5 bg-neutral-600"></div>
  <div class="relative -mx-[3%] h-3.5 rounded-b-xl bg-neutral-700 shadow-[0_16px_40px_-12px_rgb(0_0_0_/_0.3)]">
    <div class="absolute left-1/2 top-0 h-1.5 w-20 -translate-x-1/2 rounded-b-md bg-neutral-800"></div>
  </div>
</div>
